# Consulting Checklists

Working checklists for each customer meeting, condensed from the Consulting Playbook (v1.2). Use them the day before a meeting, not the morning of.

!!! info "Internal use only"
    This page is for Sensorfact staff. Don't share the password outside the team.

## Customer journey at a glance

| Phase | Meeting | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Month 1 | Asset Configuration | Get to know the customer, set up monitoring, agree objectives |
| Month 2 to 3 | Tool Optimization | Review first results, fix gaps, confirm the customer is self-sufficient |
| Every 6 months | Consultancy Check-In | Validate impact, review open incidents, check churn and upsell, plan next steps |

---

## Before any meeting

- [ ] All sensors online (flag anything offline)
- [ ] Open incidents reviewed
- [ ] Impact sheet up to date
- [ ] Notes from the previous meeting reviewed
- [ ] WebApp checked for anomalies
- [ ] Customer research done (first meeting)
- [ ] Logistics sorted: calendar invite sent, right people invited (maintenance manager included)
- [ ] Everything open and pre-loaded: WebApp, impact sheet, Dash analysis, notes

---

## 1. Asset Configuration Meeting

### Preparation

**Admin and logistics**

- [ ] Client/ticket assigned to me in Retool; monitoring alarms daily
- [ ] Velocity threshold set (ISO or asset-specific) so it can be reviewed with the customer
- [ ] Scheduling email sent within 24 hours of assignment in the Consulting HubSpot funnel
- [ ] At least three time slots offered
- [ ] Meeting scheduled within one month of ticket creation

**Customer research (20 to 30 minutes)**

- [ ] Website, LinkedIn and recent news checked
- [ ] One or two personal connection points found (region, product, milestone)
- [ ] Enough industry knowledge to ask specific, not generic, questions

**Technical**

- [ ] At least one Expert Alert sent before the meeting
- [ ] All RMS readings checked in the WebApp; standout readings noted
- [ ] Earlier Expert Alerts reviewed, customer responses checked
- [ ] Explanation of threshold adjustment prepared
- [ ] Automatic alert demo ready
- [ ] Impact sheet ready to share

### Meeting structure

| Block | Time | Focus |
|---|---|---|
| Opening | 5 to 10 min | Genuine small talk, reference your research |
| Introducing PdM | 10 min | Vibration basics, what PdM detects, use a live Expert Alert as an example |
| Asset context | 20 min | Maintenance plan, criticality, common defects, spare parts |
| WebApp and alert setup | 10 min | Key insights, automatic alerts step by step, offline sensor alerts |
| Close and next steps | 5 min | Objectives, follow-ups, next contact |

**Questions to ask**

| Topic | Example question |
|---|---|
| Maintenance plan | Do you follow a fixed maintenance schedule, or repair when things break? |
| Asset criticality | If this pump stopped, how quickly would production be affected? |
| Common defects | What tends to go wrong most often on your line? |
| Spare parts | Do you keep spares on site for critical components? |

### Goals

- [ ] Personal connection built
- [ ] Predictive Maintenance introduced and explained for their assets
- [ ] Customer journey explained (next months, your role)
- [ ] Asset context understood: maintenance plan, common defects, criticality, spare parts
- [ ] Shared objectives agreed and confirmed as deliverable
- [ ] Automatic alerts demonstrated step by step
- [ ] Offline sensor alerts set up during the meeting
- [ ] Impact so far shared, calculation explained at a high level
- [ ] Upsell opportunity noted (flag for CSM, do not push)

!!! success "Minimum you must leave with"
    - [ ] Confirmed shared objective and common definition of success
    - [ ] Asset Maintenance Profile completed or in progress
    - [ ] Automatic alerts configured and demonstrated

!!! warning "Watch out"
    Limit offline sensor troubleshooting to 5 minutes. If the cause isn't obvious, note it, inform support@sensorfact.nl, tell the customer you'll investigate internally, and schedule a follow-up if needed.

### After the meeting

- [ ] Follow-up actions confirmed with the customer
- [ ] Explainer videos sent if the customer hasn't seen them
- [ ] Upsell opportunity flagged to the CSM
- [ ] Notes documented while fresh

