## 2. Tool Optimization Meeting

### Preparation

- [ ] Earlier connection issues reviewed and status noted
- [ ] WebApp checked for missing information (sensor pictures, installation notes, shaft speeds)
- [ ] Notes, emails and the shared onboarding sheet re-read
- [ ] Automatic alerts checked: configured and sent? (If not, priority for this meeting)
- [ ] Unnecessary recurring alerts identified
- [ ] List of open incidents prepared, with impacts noted
- [ ] Impact sheet completed or updated
- [ ] Structured presentation prepared covering offline sensors, alerts, asset data, incidents, impact sheet and survey
- [ ] Satisfaction survey ready to send
- [ ] Check-In date proposed
- [ ] CSM introduction prepared (if not done yet)

### Goals

- [ ] Customer's plan of action for open Expert Alerts and Registered Incidents understood
- [ ] Six-month Check-In cycle explained and agreed
- [ ] Automatic alerts verified (set up live if missing)
- [ ] Check-In date locked in
- [ ] Planned maintenance windows discussed; Check-In date adjusted if needed
- [ ] Asset Maintenance Profile confirmed complete (agree a completion date if not)
- [ ] Customer confident using all WebApp features alone
- [ ] Satisfaction survey sent immediately at the end of the meeting
- [ ] Missing asset context collected
- [ ] CSM introduced (if not done yet)
- [ ] All sensors confirmed online; anything offline flagged

!!! success "Minimum you must leave with"
    - [ ] Expert alerts confirmed
    - [ ] Automated alerts configured
    - [ ] Consultancy Check-In date agreed and in the calendar
    - [ ] Customer self-sufficient in the WebApp, with no open questions

### Common time sinks

| Time sink | How to handle it |
|---|---|
| Offline sensors | Max 5 minutes. Ask the customer to reset, handle internally, don't troubleshoot live |
| More than 3 to 4 open incidents | Prioritise four, send the rest in a follow-up email |
| Slow loading in Retool or Dash | Keep live analysis minimal; prepare screenshots or exports in advance |
| Wrong people in the meeting | If the maintenance manager isn't there, reschedule |
| Unresolved issues from Asset Config | Address these first |

### Working agreements

- [ ] Do not agree to specific or time-consuming reports. Say instead: "I noted in my agenda that around week X I will check Pump A and inform you"
- [ ] Any maintenance window or critical asset mentioned goes straight into the calendar or task list, with an email check-in planned
- [ ] Customer understands we analyse their assets continuously, even when no Expert Alert is sent

