## 3. Consultancy Check-In (every 6 months)

### Preparation (a few days ahead)

- [ ] All sensors online (don't present a health report with half the sensors offline)
- [ ] Recent automated alerts reviewed
- [ ] All Expert Alerts since the last meeting reviewed
- [ ] Impact registered for every Expert Alert
- [ ] Concrete impact value ready to present and validate
- [ ] Impact overview with a clear story: what happened, what we caught, what it was worth
- [ ] Open incidents reviewed and status noted
- [ ] Previous meeting notes reviewed
- [ ] CSM and/or AE consulted on satisfaction and commercial situation
- [ ] At least one area identified where the customer could get more value
- [ ] Reminder sent to the customer a few days before (HubSpot reminder plus a short note)
- [ ] Maintenance window dates checked
- [ ] Next Check-In date ready to propose

### Goals

**Satisfaction and objectives**

- [ ] Asked directly: are they satisfied, what works, what doesn't
- [ ] Original objectives reviewed: met, and any new ones to add
- [ ] Product feedback and improvement suggestions invited

**WebApp usage**

- [ ] Asked what they don't know how to do
- [ ] Asked how the WebApp has supported their maintenance planning
- [ ] Missing features or improvements logged

**Open incidents**

- [ ] Each open incident reviewed: status and next steps agreed
- [ ] If too many, prioritised by criticality and the rest noted

**Impact validation**

- [ ] Impact overview walked through together, including the actions taken to reduce vibration
- [ ] Discussed whether the impact was presented at the right time
- [ ] Customer validated the figures; disagreements understood and estimates adjusted

**Updates, upsell and churn**

- [ ] Relevant WebApp updates highlighted
- [ ] Customer assessed as at risk, stable, or candidate for expansion
- [ ] Anything relevant flagged to the CSM/AE afterwards

**Next meeting**

- [ ] Next Check-In date agreed before ending the call
- [ ] Maintenance window near the proposed date checked
- [ ] If a window falls before the next meeting: shortlist of assets and components to inspect agreed
- [ ] If a window falls after: plan to review flagged assets at the Check-In

!!! success "Minimum you must leave with"
    - [ ] Customer satisfaction checked and documented
    - [ ] Impact validated (or disagreement understood)
    - [ ] Next Check-In date confirmed in the calendar

!!! info "If there was no direct impact"
    That can lead to churn. Check whether the monitored assets are really the critical ones for the customer.

### Common time sinks

| Time sink | How to handle it |
|---|---|
| Too many sensors to discuss | Go through your top 10 most concerning assets |
| Customer doesn't show up | Reminder 3 days before; on a no-show, escalate to the CSM and phone the customer |
| Missing context information | Flag it, ask the customer to fill it in during the meeting, otherwise log an action item |
| Offline sensors | Address at the start, and flag them when presenting the impact report |

