## Reference: explaining ISO standards to customers

- [ ] For most monitored machines, ISO gives the industry standard for allowable velocity RMS
- [ ] Zones A (green) and B (yellow) are acceptable
- [ ] Warning threshold sits at the B/C boundary; alarm threshold at zone D
- [ ] ISO levels are generic and ignore surroundings (several motors on one frame, crushers versus a small fan)
- [ ] So: monitor first, analyse when levels exceed ISO, and only deviate if both you and the customer agree

!!! warning "Watch out"
    Vibration above about 20 mm/s is generally perceptible as noise. Don't accept elevated levels unless you can clearly explain why; if you concede too readily, you're more likely to be held accountable when a component fails.

